From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:40:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webos-service: match LS2 filenames by suffix, not by
 substring

The ACG loop globbed "*<type>*.in" for type in (role, service), which assumes
the type word appears nowhere else in the filename. webOS service names
routinely contain "service" - com.webos.service.* is the usual convention - so
for any such component "*service*.in" matched its <name>.role.json.in as well
as its <name>.service.in.

The role file was therefore substituted twice and installed twice: once into
roles.d, correctly, and once into services.d, where a role JSON is not a
D-Bus service file and has no business being. On LuneOS this put a stray
com.webos.service.ime.role.json in services.d on every image.

Matching the whole suffix instead - *.role.json.in and *.service.in - is exact
for both types and for every naming convention in the tree, including the
components whose names do not contain "service" at all. Verified with qmake
against com.webos.service.ime.*, com.palm.smtp.* and browser-shell.*.

The parallel loop below for perm/api/group already anchors its glob with a
leading dot ("*.<type>*.json"), so it never had this problem and is left
alone. An unhandled type now errors out rather than silently reusing the
previous iteration's pattern.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 features/webos-service.prf | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/features/webos-service.prf b/features/webos-service.prf
index db65542..cc613a5 100644
--- a/features/webos-service.prf
+++ b/features/webos-service.prf
@@ -117,8 +117,19 @@ group.path = $$WEBOS_INSTALL_SYSBUS_GROUPDIR
     SYSBUS_FILE_TYPE_IN = role service
     SYSBUS_FILE_TYPE = perm api group
 
+    # Match the whole filename suffix rather than "*<type>*". webOS service
+    # names routinely contain "service" themselves - com.webos.service.* is the
+    # usual convention - so "*service*.in" also matched that component's
+    # <name>.role.json.in, and the role file was substituted and installed a
+    # second time, into services.d alongside the real .service file.
     for (type, SYSBUS_FILE_TYPE_IN) {
-        found_files = $$files("$$WEBOS_SYSBUS_DIR/*$$type*.in")
+        unset(SYSBUS_GLOB_IN)
+        equals(type, role):    SYSBUS_GLOB_IN = *.role.json.in
+        equals(type, service): SYSBUS_GLOB_IN = *.service.in
+        isEmpty(SYSBUS_GLOB_IN): \
+            error("webos-service: no filename pattern defined for LS2 file type '$$type'")
+
+        found_files = $$files("$$WEBOS_SYSBUS_DIR/$$SYSBUS_GLOB_IN")
         !isEmpty(found_files) {
             message("Found SYSBUS_FILE_TYPE_IN: $$found_files")
             QMAKE_SUBSTITUTES += $$found_files
